\section{Deployment}
Four wooden nesting blocks were mounted on garage walls in the Riverside and Hillcrest districts.
Each block held sixty paper tubes of two diameters.
Blocks were inspected on the first weekend of each month from October to April.
Section~\ref{sec:winter} summarizes emergence outcomes by orientation.

\begin{figure}[t]
\centering
\fbox{\parbox{0.72\linewidth}{\centering Sketch of the four nesting blocks A--D, their height above ground, and the orientation of the entrance holes.}}
\caption{Layout of the four nesting blocks on the garage walls.}
\label{fig:boxes}
\end{figure}

Tubes were weighed at installation and again at the April opening.
Emergence was scored by counting opened mud caps over three weeks in spring.
